<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Lal Dhang</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1774</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rohilla-war">Rohilla War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Lal Dhang was concluded in October 1774 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shuja-ud-daula">Shuja-ud-Daula</a>, Nawab of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/awadh">Awadh</a>, and the Rohilla chief <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/faizullah-khan">Faizullah Khan</a> at the end of the First <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rohilla-war">Rohilla War</a>. After Awadh and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> troops had defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rohillas">Rohillas</a> at Miranpur Katra, Faizullah Khan, who had retreated to Lal Dhang in the foothills, was allowed to keep Rampur and the surrounding districts. The settlement founded the princely state of Rampur.</p></div>
